              the  connection to the server. Multiple instances are permitted,
              to allow setting of both the IPv4 and IPv6 source addresses.

       --cc ccoonnffiigg--ffiillee
              This option indicates ccoonnffiigg--ffiillee as the configuration file  in‐
              stead of the default, ////eettcc//rrnnddcc..ccoonnff.

       --kk kkeeyy--ffiillee
              This  option  indicates  kkeeyy--ffiillee as the key file instead of the
              default, ////eettcc//rrnnddcc..kkeeyy. The  key  in  @@ssyyssccoonnffddiirr@@//rrnnddcc..kkeeyy  is
              used  to  authenticate  commands  sent to the server if the con‐
